From db76f291e1163124f75c19520cce56fbd5cec862 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brendan Juno <brendan@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:53:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add grouped-companion inventory cleanup

Bots grouped with a real player sell grey junk and outgrown white or
green gear when a vendor is already within 20 yards, even if their bags
are not nearly full. Opening a vendor (or gossip on a vendor NPC) makes
nearby grouped bots sell too. .botcmd inventory <guid|all> and the
COABOT INVENTORY verb force the same sweep and report gold earned.
Blues and better are kept unless bags are down to two free slots.
The command and vendor-open hook never destroy items in the field;
destruction without a vendor still only happens when bags are completely
full. Sales honor OnPlayerCanSellItem. New keys (all default on):
CoaBots.Inventory.SellWhenNearVendor, SellOnLeaderVendor, KeepQuality=3.
